# Punar scheduled reconcile (milestone-4.md §6): one full section-42 pass
# (observe → … → apply → verify → audit → compliance), driven by
# punard-reconcile.timer. Deliberately a plain root `punarctl` through the
# normal socket — the timer REUSES the audited request surface instead of an
# internal daemon thread (which would be an always-on wakeup source, invisible
# to systemctl list-timers, and an unaudited trigger path). Honest limit
# (ipc.md section 6): the daemon sees only peer credentials, so these runs
# audit as user_id "root", source "human" — indistinguishable from an admin.
#
# No User= — reconcile is root-only (ipc.md 5.6). Not [Install]-enabled
# itself; the .timer carries the vendor-wants symlink.

[Unit]
Description=Punar scheduled reconcile (drift remediation)
After=punard.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/punarctl --json reconcile
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
